 "title": "GIS | Meeker County, MN - Official Website",
 "text": "GIS | Meeker County, MN - Official Website\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nAlert!\nMEEKER COUNTY HAS A NEW WEB ADDRESS\nRead On For Details...\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nGovernment\nServices\nOur County\nHow Do I...?\n-->\nHome\nGovernment\nGovernment Offices\nHighway\nGIS\nGIS\nMeeker County Geographic Information Systems (GIS) is a division of the Land Use Records (Planning/Zoning) Department. It is a computer system used for capturing, storing, checking and displaying data related to positions on the Earth's surface.\nGIS can show many different kinds of data on one map. This enables people to more easily see, analyze, and understand patterns and relationships.\nDisclaimer: This data is made available on an \"as is\" basis, without express or implied warranty of any sort including, specifically, any implied warranties of fitness for a particular purpose, warranties of merchantability or warranties relating to the accuracy or completeness of the database(s).\nMeeker County GIS Tool\nBeacon Property Tool\nContact Information\nTeresa Lieser\n320-693-5718\nComprehensive Local Water Plan Update\nGrant Posting Requirements\nPlanning Commission\nBoard of Adjustment\nGIS\nOne Watershed One Plan (1W1P)\nSign up for Updates\nApply for Employment\nPay Online\nReserve a Facility\nTax & Parcel Search\n-->\nAll photos by Robyn Richardson\nContact Us\n114 N Holcombe Ave. Ste 160\nLitchfield, MN 55355\nStaff Directory\nCounty Facebook Pages\nEconomic Development\nHistorical Society\nHumane Society\nMeeker County\nOffice of the Meeker County Sheriff\nMeeker County Public Works\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHOME\nSITE MAP\nACCESSIBILITY\nCOPYRIGHT NOTICES\nGOVERNMENT WEBSITES BY CIVICPLUS®\n/QuickLinks.aspx\n-->\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
